From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quoc Trinh <quoc.trinh.fz@renesas.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Jul 2026 07:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pvr_fence: guard fence_value_str (removed in kernel 6.16)

The PowerVR fence tracepoints in pvr_fence_trace.h call
dma_fence_ops::fence_value_str, but that callback was removed from
struct dma_fence_ops in Linux v6.16. On the team's linux-yocto V4H
kernel (6.18.20, built with KCONFIG_MODE=alldefconfig which enables
CONFIG_EVENT_TRACING), the TRACE_EVENT macros expand these TP_fast_assign
blocks for real, so the now-missing member fails do_compile:

  pvr_fence_trace.h:119: error: 'const struct dma_fence_ops' has no
  member named 'fence_value_str'

(The rcar-community linux-renesas build did not hit this only because its
config left event tracing off, so the macro bodies were never compiled.)

Guard the three fence_value_str uses behind a version check, mirroring
the driver's own existing pvr_assign_str KERNEL_VERSION guard. For
kernels >= 6.16 the trace records just carry "unknown" for the fence
value string (a debug-only field), which is exactly the fallback the
driver already uses for foreign fences when the callback is absent.

Upstream-Status: Pending [PowerVR closed-source DDK, kernel 6.16 port]

Signed-off-by: Quoc Trinh <quoc.trinh.fz@renesas.com>
---
 services/server/env/linux/pvr_fence_trace.h | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/server/env/linux/pvr_fence_trace.h b/services/server/env/linux/pvr_fence_trace.h
--- a/services/server/env/linux/pvr_fence_trace.h
+++ b/services/server/env/linux/pvr_fence_trace.h
@@ -116,8 +116,13 @@
 			fence->base.ops->get_driver_name(&fence->base));
 		pvr_assign_str(timeline,
 			fence->base.ops->get_timeline_name(&fence->base));
+#if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6, 16, 0))
 		fence->base.ops->fence_value_str(&fence->base,
 			__entry->val, sizeof(__entry->val));
+#else
+		(void) OSStringSafeCopy(__entry->val,
+			"unknown", sizeof(__entry->val));
+#endif
 		__entry->context = fence->base.context;
 	),

@@ -175,8 +180,13 @@
 			fence->base.ops->get_driver_name(&fence->base));
 		pvr_assign_str(timeline,
 			fence->base.ops->get_timeline_name(&fence->base));
+#if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6, 16, 0))
 		fence->base.ops->fence_value_str(&fence->base, __entry->val,
 			sizeof(__entry->val));
+#else
+		(void) OSStringSafeCopy(__entry->val,
+			"unknown", sizeof(__entry->val));
+#endif
 		__entry->context = fence->base.context;
 		pvr_assign_str(foreign_driver,
 			fence->fence->ops->get_driver_name ?
@@ -186,12 +196,17 @@
 			fence->fence->ops->get_timeline_name ?
 			fence->fence->ops->get_timeline_name(fence->fence) :
 			"unknown");
+#if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6, 16, 0))
 		fence->fence->ops->fence_value_str ?
 			fence->fence->ops->fence_value_str(
 				fence->fence, __entry->foreign_val,
 				sizeof(__entry->foreign_val)) :
 			(void) OSStringSafeCopy(__entry->foreign_val,
 				"unknown", sizeof(__entry->foreign_val));
+#else
+		(void) OSStringSafeCopy(__entry->foreign_val,
+			"unknown", sizeof(__entry->foreign_val));
+#endif
 		__entry->foreign_context = fence->fence->context;
 	),

--
